;
; How Flint files one command in its history, in MYRA: the command's
; number, when it ran (Unix seconds), its exit status (0 ran, 1 refused, 2
; misused, 127 no such command, as sh counts them) and the command line's
; length in bytes. Flint asks whether the numbers fit before it records.
^ZXFLINT(seq:i9) = stamp:i12! ^ status:i3! ^ bytes:i4!
